%%label I. Allegro con brio
%%note A major, mostly in 7/8 (2+2+3). A curtain-raiser states the quartet's motto (two rising fourths and a falling third); the first theme passes from first violin to viola over a plucked cello figure; a 5/8 transition leads to a sung second theme in C major built from the same two fourths. The development is a fugato whose climax plays both themes at once; the second theme returns in A.
X:1
T:Bernstein’s Missing Quartet
T:I. Allegro con brio
C:Lor, in the manner of Leonard Bernstein
M:7/8
L:1/8
Q:"Allegro con brio" 1/4=132
%%score [1 | 2 | 3 | 4]
V:1 clef=treble name="Vl. I"
V:2 clef=treble name="Vl. II"
V:3 clef=alto name="Vla."
V:4 clef=bass name="Vc."
K:A
V:1
